at there are thousands of people that  have um ignored that advice and i  suppose their logic is is that they're  already fearful of their lives um so you  know they've chosen to stay that's  that's not what we would advise them to  do i think it's right that we've told  them that the intelligence is so  credible now and so imminent that we  think they should move away  but we're doing our best to keep those  that have  not left safe  we're doing our best to look at what  other alternative provisions  we might be able to make but obviously  we won't be advertising those because  that would simply make the alternative  routes  a target in themselves  islamic state in the karazhan provinces  is acutely aware of the fact that there  is a closing window for people to leave  that is concentrating people uh in  towards the airport and that is giving  them an opportunity to do something that  they would regard as spectacular  we would regard as absolutely abhorrent  um but it means we have to be very clear  with people what the risks are and we're  doing our best to mitigate them but it's  not we don't have the number of troops  on the ground that we would need to be  able to go off into the city find the  threat and remove it um and that means  therefore we have to  try to operate within the threat  envelope as it is and do our best to get  as many people out as we can at the time  that remains  um i wonder then if you you you'll  probably be aware of the situation  regarding at least one uh british  national pen farthing has been something  i've thought on the mod side over the  past couple of days but he has been  tweeting that he is near to the airport  with his afghan staff the taliban are  not letting him through  he is a british national is there any  argument for putting british troops  outside of the wire to try and get him  and potentially even his staff to safety  so for for him uh i mean  it is  a grim reality of these situations that  uh as a british national 